    introHeading: "What a refrigerator call looks like in Irvine.",
    introHtml: `<p>Irvine refrigerators split by village. Through the Woodbridge, Northwood, Woodbury and Portola Springs tracts it's mid-tier Samsung, LG, Whirlpool and GE units from the master-planned build-out — condenser-fan failures, defrost faults, and the sealed-system issues that hit certain linear-compressor models. Up in the Turtle Rock, Quail Hill and Shady Canyon estates it's built-in Sub-Zero and Viking columns where a dust-clogged condenser or a failed evaporator fan has one zone drifting warm. The coastal OC climate is mild, but a Santa Ana week still spikes the load on an already-marginal condenser.</p>
<p>Our guys stock Samsung, LG, Whirlpool and GE parts on the truck and stage Sub-Zero and Viking sealed-system parts for the estate calls. On a warm-fridge visit we check the sealed system, defrost and fans together — from the kitchen a condenser failure and a defrost fault look identical, and only one is the real cause. $89 residential diagnostic, off the invoice with the repair.</p>`,
    honest: `<p>Math on refrigerators: a mid-tier unit 12-plus years old with a dead compressor is usually a replace, and you'll hear that from us before we charge a diagnostic. Where repair is the easy call is the built-ins: a Sub-Zero column is an $8,000-plus unit, and a $600-to-900 condenser or evaporator job buys another decade — worth it every time in an estate kitchen you're not rebuilding.</p>
<p>The one we flag is the sealed-system leak on 2015-2019 LG and Samsung linear compressors — common in Irvine's newer tract homes. That's a genuine repair, not a replace, but it has to be brazed and recharged by someone EPA-608 certified, or it's warm inside again within a month.</p>`,
