    introHtml: `<p>Irvine's washers are mostly newer front-load LG and Samsung and top-load Whirlpool and Maytag from the master-planned build-out through Woodbridge, Northwood, Woodbury and Westpark. The front-loaders throw drain-pump clogs, worn door boots and the occasional bad bearing; the top-loaders drop lid switches, drive couplers and worn suspensions. The Ranch district's hard water plays here too — scale on the inlet valve shows up as a slow or uneven fill.</p>
<p>Our guys carry drain pumps, door boots, lid switches, couplers and inlet valves on the truck, so a single-fault washer call is usually one visit. When a washer "won't drain," we pull the pump filter first — it's coins, hairpins and lint far more often than a dead pump — so you're not charged for a part you didn't need. $89 residential diagnostic, off the bill with the repair.</p>`,
